    "title": "quantyra-null-cone-lean: finite causal-order rank rigidity",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23202763",
    "publication_date": "2026-10-07",
    "description": "<p>Lean 4 proof of finite realizer rank rigidity: for every two-order realizer of an occupied-grid sample, one global axis exchange gives both interior rank errors at most 30rn under explicit marginal and boundary hypotheses.</p><p>The accompanying draft preprint derives d_conf &lt;= 100 (N^(-1/12) + Delta_N) for a restricted smooth positive uniform-marginal density class in a two-dimensional conformal diamond. Only the deterministic finite theorem is Lean verified. Probability, continuous-density interpolation and proper-time comparisons remain prose proofs. Novelty and independent review are unconfirmed; no general spacetime reconstruction, new physical law, curvature estimate or carrying-capacity benefit is claimed.</p><p>Software and proof code: Apache-2.0. The files under manuscript/ are licensed CC-BY-4.0 as stated in manuscript/README.md and LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt.</p>",
